        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: باریدن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "باریدن (bâridan) — \"to rain, to fall (of rain or snow)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تمام شب باران بارید. Tamâm-e shab bârân bârid. It rained all night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present stem bâr-: bârân mibârad — it is raining. Snow too: barf bârid."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bâridan is a native verb on the same stem as bârân 'rain', which is usually traced to Middle Persian wārān. EtymDB does not list the verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
