              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رگبار (ragbâr) — \"a downpour, a heavy shower\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "یک رگبار تند آمد و همه خیس شدیم. Yek ragbâr-e tond âmad va hame khis shodim. A heavy shower came and we all got wet."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also a burst of gunfire."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ragbâr is usually analysed as native rag 'vein, streak' and bâr 'raining', the stem of bâridan: rain falling in streaks. EtymDB does not list it."
            }
          ]
        },
